"Flowers": {
  "index": 5,
  "category": "basics",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Flowers"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "There are certain flowers that grow around the world that I'll need in order to make the most use of magic. These flowers are often used as reagents or ingredients, so I should take note of where to find them.\n\nAll of these flowers can be crushed into dyes, some of the colors being particularly hard to find otherwise.\n\nI can also trade with "
        },
        {
          "text": "Spellmongers",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " in "
        },
        {
          "text": "villages",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " for "
        },
        {
          "text": "Herbalist Pouches",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " for these flowers if I do not wish to locate them myself. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Aum",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "location": "mna:aum",
      "scale": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Sometimes known as the 'lily of life', "
        },
        {
          "text": "Aum",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " are found in "
        },
        {
          "text": "Forests and Plains",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". They often have uses in healing and restorative endeavors despite their extremely bitter taste."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Cerublossom",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "location": "mna:cerublossom",
      "scale": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "An extremely common flower, "
        },
        {
          "text": "Cerublossom ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "are often mistaken for a blue orchid at a glance. However, they do have a telltale shimmer at closer inspection. They can be found in "
        },
        {
          "text": "forests, plains, and wintery places",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Cerublossom are used in a wide variety of magical recipes. It's been said that they can emit a soothing hum that can only be heard by young children."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Tarma Root",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "location": "mna:tarma_root",
      "scale": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Tarma Root ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "grow in large quantities in "
        },
        {
          "text": "swamps",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Their sharp thorns make them uncomfortable to pick and nearly impossible to eat. The way these roots can sway in the wind has lead to stories about them granting the ability to fly. This, however, has never been accomplished and is widely believed to be nothing more than a legend."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Desert Nova",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "location": "mna:desert_nova",
      "scale": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "As their namesake suggests, "
        },
        {
          "text": "Desert Nova ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "grow in "
        },
        {
          "text": "warm sandy regions",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Even on the coldest desert night they are warm to the touch, and have been used by many to keep warm by keeping a few in their pockets."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Wakebloom",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "location": "mna:wakebloom",
      "scale": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Wakebloom ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "thrive in "
        },
        {
          "text": "water",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", growing as small seeds along the ocean floors and riverbeds before floating up to the top of the water and blooming in a beautiful fashion. They carry a surprising amount of water with them even when harvested."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
